of low extremity shows occlusion of the right popliteal artery.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjfm-32-423-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Arteriography shows occlusion of the right popliteal artery before intervention at left side figure and show restored blood flow after removal by thombosuction at right side.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjfm-32-423-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>The paroxymsmal atrial fibrillation was shown on electrocardiogram, when she visited an emergency room with palpitation.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjfm-32-423-g003"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>The rhythm was converted to normal sinus rhythm after twelve hours on the same day.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjfm-32-423-g004"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Clinical manifestation and arteriographic finding of acute arterial embolism versus thrombosis.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjfm-32-423-i001"/></table-wrap></floats-group></article>